    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet discreetly back from Leopardstown Road, Castlemoyle is an impressive detached family residence nestled within magnificent, mature gardens extending to just under half an acre.\n\nThis exceptional home has been thoughtfully designed to meet the demands of contemporary family living, offering a wonderful balance of elegant reception rooms and comfortable everyday spaces. An attractive portico entrance opens to a bright and welcoming hallway, where classic panelled walls and crema Marfil stone flooring create an immediate sense of warmth and understated luxury. A spacious cloakroom and beautifully appointed guest WC add both practicality and style.\n\nTo the right, the dining room, with its generous bay window overlooking the front garden, flows seamlessly into the drawing room. Here, a contemporary limestone fireplace provides an interesting focal point, while double doors lead out to the rear patio ideal for for entertaining.\n\nA cosy snug/TV room provides an intimate retreat for quieter moments, while the larger dual-aspect family room with dual aspect provides a relaxed setting for everyday living. It enjoys a bay window to the front and a white marble fireplace with black inset and coal-effect gas fire, this inviting space is perfectly suited to family gatherings and sporting occasions.\n\nThe kitchen/breakfast room forms the true heart of the home. Bathed in natural light from a charming curved glazed window and opening to the patio via French doors, it is both functional and welcoming. A central island enhances the layout, making it ideal for casual dining and socialising.\n\nUpstairs, the first floor boasts five generously proportioned bedrooms (main ensuite). A spacious landing, with three large light wells ensures this space if bathed in light throughout the day and enhances the sense of space and light throughout. Extensive built-in wardrobes and a well-appointed linen cupboard provide excellent storage.\n\nSurrounded by beautifully established gardens and enjoying a highly convenient location within walking distance of the LUAS at Sandyford/Central Park and the N11, Castlemoyle represents a rare opportunity to acquire a truly exceptional family home in a prime setting.\n\nLocated just a stroll to the LUAS stop at Sandyford/Central Park and the N11. An excellent selection of schools are nearby. These include Hollypark Boys and Girls National School, St Brigid's Boys and Girls National School and many of South County Dublin's Secondary Schools to include Blackrock College, Mount Anville, Loreto Foxrock, Lycee Francais d'Irlande as well as the newly opened Nord Anglia International School and St Andrew's College all just a short commute away.\n\nOUTSIDE:\nEnjoying a private and mature setting on just under half an acre of gardens (0.458 acres approximately). High perimeter wall on the outer boundaries provides excellent privacy. Spacious tarmacadamed driveway with parking for several cars. Wrap-around garden on three sides. Large front garden lawn with feature gravelled pathways. Mature, private and landscaped with eucalyptus trees and mature shrubs. Pergola with climbing honeysuckle to the side garden with children's play area to include swings. Raised patio area to the back with lawned grass and gravelled pathway to a barna shed."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPortico - \nTwo granite steps to the portico with supporting columns lead to the hall door.\n\nEntrance Hall - \nHall door flanked on either side buy stained glass floor to ceiling windows. Crema Marfil flooring. Stairs with understairs storage.\n\nHome Office/Study - \nBuilt-in desk with shelving. Floor to ceiling window. Dual aspect. Wide plank oak flooring.\n\nGuest Toliet - \nPanelled walls. “Visions” sink. Toilet.\n\nCloaks/Boot Room - \nExtensive storage.\n\nDining room - \nDual aspect with bay to front and window to side. Opens to:\n\nDrawing Room - \nContemporary limestone fireplace and hearth. Sliding doors to patio to the rear.\n\nTV/Snug Room - \nBuilt-in entertainment unit with presses, drawers and shelving.\n\nLiving/Family Room - \nTwo gentle steps descend to this bright, dual aspect room with bay window to the front. White marble fireplace with black marble inset. Coal effect gas fire. With pale limed oak flooring.\n\nKitchen / Breakfast Room - \nAlno kitchen with wall and floor presses. Neff double oven, ceramic hob and microwave. Franke stainless steel sink unit. Fisher Paykal fridge freezer. Feature curved bay seating area. Skylight. French doors to the patio to the rear.\n\nUtility Room - \nWall and floor units. Domec circular stainless steel sink unit. Hot press with water tank. Plumbed for washing machine. Door to back\n\nBedroom 2 - \nDouble to the front with mahogany effect flooring. Built-in wardrobes.\n\nFamily Room - \nIdeal Standard wash hand basin in floating vanity unit. Toilet with back to wall pan. Heated towel rail. Corner shower with Triton T-90 electric shower. Free standing bath with wall attached hand held shower. Ceramic tiled walls with recessed shampoo shelf.Half landing with steps to main landing with 3 large light wells and a row of fitted wardrobes providing excellent storage space and incorporating a linen cupboard.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nDouble with fitted wardrobe.\n\nDormer Space - \nCurrently configured as sleeping space.\n\nShower room - \nChocolate coloured stone effect ceramic tiled floor. Toilet with back to wall pan. Wash hand basin in vanity unit. Shower with rainbow shower and handheld shower attachment, recessed shampoo shelf. Radiator cabinet.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nLarge twin to the back. Extensive built-in wardrobes with desk unit and shelving.\n\nMain Bedroom - \nLarge bay window overlooking the garden to the front. Fitted wardrobes.\n\nEn-Suite - \nShower with rainbow shower and handheld shower attachment. Recessed shampoo shelf. Window to the front. Toilet with back to wall pan.\n\nBedroom 5 - \nOverlooking the front. Storage unit which doubles as a seat with cushion. Dormer window.\n\nEn-Suite - \nCeramic tiled shower, pedestal wash hand basin and toilet with back to wall pan.\n\n"
      },
